$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure H for the Preparation of Benzanilide Inhibitor
Intermediates: To a scintillation vial equipped with a stir bar was
combined the amine (0.15 mmol, 1.0 equiv) and the Boc protected acid
coupling partner (59 mg, 0.29 mmol, 2.0 equiv) in THF (0.50 mL, 0.30 M).
EDCI hydrochloride (29 mg, 0.15 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was subsequently added.
The reaction progress was monitored by LC-MS. Complete conversion of the
amine starting material to product was observed after approximately 1 h.
The solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the crude residue was
then dissolved in a 1:1 mixture of TFA:CH2Cl2 (4.0 mL total). After 1 h,
the solvent was removed and the crude residue was lyophilized for one
hour to remove trace TFA. The crude amines were used without further
purification. General Warhead Addition Procedure I for the Preparation of
Inhibitors The crude amines were dissolved in MeOH at a concentration of
0.10 M in a round bottom flask equipped with a stir bar. Triethylamine
(4.0 equiv) was added to the reaction mixture. Ethyl 2-chloroacetimidate
hydrochloride (4.0 equiv) was subsequently added, and the mixture was
stirred at rt until completion as determined by LC-MS (20 min to 1 h).
The solvent was removed, and purification by reverse-phase column
chromatography (gradient: 10% MeCN to 100% MeCN in H2O + 0.1% TFA)
followed by subsequent lyophilization. The products as TFA salts.
Inhibitor 5b: Coupling of commercially available benzylamine by procedure
H, followed by warhead addition by procedure I. 5b in 75% overall yield.
1H-NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD d-4): δ 7.33-7.24 (m, 5H), 4.37 (s, 2H), 4.36 (s,
2H), 3.36 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 2.38 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 1.96 (quin, J =
7.2 Hz, 2H). 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CD3OD): δ 174.56, 164.79, 139.88, 129.56,
128.59, 128.27, 44.19, 43.38, 40.11, 33.07, 24.29. HRMS (For C13H19ClN3O,
MH+): Calc’d 268.1217, found 268.1220.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM HPLC purification (final stage)
